{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,360p' src/cljd/dao/stream/cbor/cljd.cljd; rg -n 'dao\\\\.stream\\\\.cbor|cbor/' src test docs/design --glob '\"'!docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md'\"'; rg -n 'boring' . --glob '\"'!collab/**'\"' --glob '\"'!archive/**'\"' --glob '\"'!docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"(ns dao.stream.cbor.cljd\n  \"The Dart half of the `dao.stream.cbor` codec, over the pub.dev `cbor`\n   package (pinned 6.5.1) — no hand-rolled binary parser.\n\n   The wrapper, not the dependency, owns the closed portable domain and its\n   byte-level agreement with Boring on the JVM and ClojureScript:\n\n   * tag 39 identifiers (`:ns/name` text, colon-prefixed for keywords),\n   * tag 258 sets and the `clojure/with-meta` tag 27 frame for metadata,\n   * the stream's own `dao.stream/list` tag 27 frame (payload\n     `[metadata elements]`) keeping lists distinct from vectors,\n   * definite-length containers, bytewise-sorted map keys and set elements,\n     shortest lossless floats — Boring's `:canonical` rules.\n\n   Decoding additionally re-encodes and byte-compares: the package\n   materializes maps through Dart `Map`s (last write wins), so duplicate map\n   keys on the wire are detected here rather than silently collapsed.\"\n  (:require [\"package:cbor/cbor.dart\" :as cbor]\n            [clojure.string :as str])\n  (:import [\"dart:core\" Type]\n           [\"dart:typed_data\" Uint8List]))\n\n\n(def safe-integer-limit 9007199254740991)\n\n\n(defn- no-tags?\n  [v]\n  (zero? (count (.-tags v))))\n\n\n(defn- only-tag?\n  \"True when v carries exactly one tag and it is `t`.\"\n  [v t]\n  (and (= 1 (count (.-tags v))) (= t (nth (.-tags v) 0))))\n\n\n(defn- bytes-compare\n  \"Bytewise order, a proper prefix sorting first — Boring's canonical rule.\"\n  [a b]\n  (let [n (min (count a) (count b))]\n    (loop [i 0]\n      (if (= i n)\n        (- (count a) (count b))\n        (let [d (- (nth a i) (nth b i))]\n          (if (zero? d) (recur (inc i)) d))))))\n\n\n(defn- bytes=\n  [a b]\n  (and (= (count a) (count b)) (zero? (bytes-compare a b))))\n\n\n(defn- in-canonical-order\n  \"Reorder encoded items by each item's own encoded bytes: set elements\n   directly, map entries by their encoded key.\"\n  [items item->cbor]\n  (->> items\n       (mapv (fn [item] [(cbor/cborEncode (item->cbor item)) item]))\n       (sort (fn [a b] (bytes-compare (first a) (first b))))\n       (mapv second)))\n\n\n(defn strip-constructor-meta\n  \"Drop ClojureDart's own compiler metadata: the call-site map whose `:tag`\n   value is a Dart `Type` (every `(list ...)` call result carries one).\n   That metadata is compiler emission, never user data — a user's own\n   `with-meta` replaces it wholesale — and treating it as data would both\n   reject fresh Dart lists from the portable domain and diverge from the\n   frozen Boring bytes.  The `:tag` Type is the marker, and only it: the\n   tag-less `{:line ... :column ... :end-line ... :end-column ...}` map is\n   this codebase's reader-position metadata, carried on every host, and\n   crosses the wire like any other user data.\"\n  [m]\n  (if (and (map? m) (dart/is? (:tag m) Type))\n    nil\n    m))\n\n\n(defn byte-payload?\n  \"True for the host byte payload the codec writes as a CBOR byte string\n   (major type 2): Uint8List here, Boring's byte[]/Uint8Array elsewhere.\"\n  [x]\n  (dart/is? x Uint8List))\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; Encoding: portable value -> CborValue tree -> canonical bytes\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n(defn- identifier-text\n  \"The tag 39 text for one identifier: Boring's colon-prefix + slash-joined\n   form.  The domain gate has already rejected identifiers this form cannot\n   round-trip.\"\n  [x]\n  (let [body (if-some [ns (namespace x)]\n               (str ns \"/\" (name x))\n               (name x))]\n    (if (keyword? x) (str \":\" body) body)))\n\n\n(declare to-cbor)\n\n\n(defn- definite-list\n  [items]\n  (cbor/CborList. items .type cbor/CborLengthType.definite))\n\n\n(defn- named-frame\n  \"One tag 27 frame: [name payload].\"\n  [name payload]\n  (cbor/CborList.\n    [(cbor/CborString. name) payload]\n    .tags [27]\n    .type cbor/CborLengthType.definite))\n\n\n(defn- to-cbor-set\n  [x]\n  (cbor/CborList. (in-canonical-order (mapv to-cbor x) identity)\n                  .tags [258]\n                  .type cbor/CborLengthType.definite))\n\n\n(defn- to-cbor-map\n  [x]\n  (let [entries (in-canonical-order\n                  (mapv (fn [entry]\n                          [(to-cbor (key entry)) (to-cbor (val entry))])\n                        x)\n                  first)]\n    ;; fromIterables, not fromEntries + MapEntry interop: ClojureDart's\n    ;; MapEntry constructor satisfies no MapEntry<CborValue,CborValue>\n    ;; generic bound, and dart:core's Map.fromIterables re-pairs the two\n    ;; already-sorted sequences without one.\n    (cbor/CborMap.fromIterables\n      (mapv first entries)\n      (mapv second entries)\n      .type cbor/CborLengthType.definite)))\n\n\n(defn to-cbor\n  \"Build the CborValue tree for one portable value.\"\n  [x]\n  (cond\n    (nil? x) (cbor/CborNull.)\n    (true? x) (cbor/CborBool. true)\n    (false? x) (cbor/CborBool. false)\n    (int? x) (cbor/CborSmallInt. x)\n    (double? x) (cbor/CborFloat. x)\n    (string? x) (cbor/CborString. x)\n    ;; before the identifier branch and as a plain value: a host byte\n    ;; payload is a CBOR byte string (major 2), never a tagged carrier —\n    ;; Boring writes its byte-string type the same way, so the bytes agree\n    (dart/is? x Uint8List) (cbor/CborBytes. x)\n    (or (keyword? x) (symbol? x))\n    ;; `when`, not `and`: if-some binds false as a value, and a keyword's\n    ;; (symbol? x) guard must reduce to nil, never a false \"metadata\" map.\n    (if-some [m (when (symbol? x)\n                  (some-> (meta x) strip-constructor-meta))]\n      (named-frame\n        \"clojure/with-meta\"\n        (definite-list [(to-cbor m) (cbor/CborString. (identifier-text x) .tags [39])]))\n      (cbor/CborString. (identifier-text x) .tags [39]))\n    (list? x) (named-frame\n                \"dao.stream/list\"\n                (definite-list [(to-cbor (some-> (meta x) strip-constructor-meta))\n                                (definite-list (mapv to-cbor x))]))\n    (vector? x) (if-some [m (some-> (meta x) strip-constructor-meta)]\n                  (named-frame\n                    \"clojure/with-meta\"\n                    (definite-list [(to-cbor m) (definite-list (mapv to-cbor x))]))\n                  (definite-list (mapv to-cbor x)))\n    (set? x) (if-some [m (some-> (meta x) strip-constructor-meta)]\n               (named-frame\n                 \"clojure/with-meta\"\n                 (definite-list [(to-cbor m) (to-cbor-set x)]))\n               (to-cbor-set x))\n    (map? x) (if-some [m (some-> (meta x) strip-constructor-meta)]\n               (named-frame\n                 \"clojure/with-meta\"\n                 (definite-list [(to-cbor m) (to-cbor-map x)]))\n               (to-cbor-map x))\n    :else (throw (ex-info \"value is outside the dao.stream.cbor portable domain\"\n                          {:value x}))))\n\n\n(defn encode\n  \"Encode one portable value as canonical CBOR bytes.\"\n  [value]\n  (Uint8List.fromList (cbor/cborEncode (to-cbor value))))\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; Decoding: bytes -> CborValue tree -> portable value\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n(defn- out-of-profile\n  [detail]\n  (throw (ex-info \"cbor value outside the stream profile\" detail)))\n\n\n(defn- from-tag39\n  \"Rebuild an identifier from its tag 39 text, splitting the namespace at the\n   first slash exactly as Boring's reader does.\"\n  [s]\n  (let [body (if (str/starts-with? s \":\") (subs s 1) s)\n        slash (str/index-of body \"/\")]\n    (if slash\n      ((if (str/starts-with? s \":\") keyword symbol)\n       (subs body 0 slash) (subs body (inc slash)))\n      ((if (str/starts-with? s \":\") keyword symbol) body))))\n\n\n(declare from-cbor)\n\n\n(defn- from-named-frame\n  \"Decode one tag 27 frame: the stream's two names only.\"\n  [name payload]\n  (let [name (str name)]\n    (when-not (or (= name \"dao.stream/list\") (= name \"clojure/with-meta\"))\n      (out-of-profile {:frame name}))\n    (when-not (= 2 (count payload))\n      (out-of-profile {:frame name}))\n    (if (= name \"dao.stream/list\")\n      (let [metadata (nth payload 0)\n            elements (nth payload 1)]\n        (when-not (dart/is? elements cbor/CborList)\n          (out-of-profile {:frame name}))\n        ;; with-meta nil clears ClojureDart's constructor metadata, so a\n        ;; metadata-free decoded list matches every other host's.\n        (with-meta (apply list (mapv from-cbor elements))\n          (from-cbor metadata)))\n      (with-meta (from-cbor (nth payload 1)) (from-cbor (nth payload 0))))))\n\n\n(defn from-cbor\n  \"Convert one CborValue into the portable domain, rejecting everything the\n   profile does not define.\"\n  [v]\n  (cond\n    (dart/is? v cbor/CborNull)\n    (if (no-tags? v) nil (out-of-profile {:value v}))\n\n    (dart/is? v cbor/CborBool)\n    (if (no-tags? v) (.-value v) (out-of-profile {:value v}))\n\n    (dart/is? v cbor/CborSmallInt)\n    (if (no-tags? v)\n      (let [n (.-value v)]\n        (if (<= (- safe-integer-limit) n safe-integer-limit)\n          n\n          (out-of-profile {:int n})))\n      (out-of-profile {:value v}))\n\n    (dart/is? v cbor/CborFloat)\n    (if (no-tags? v) (.-value v) (out-of-profile {:value v}))\n\n    (dart/is? v cbor/CborString)\n    (cond\n      (no-tags? v) (str v)\n      (only-tag? v 39) (from-tag39 (str v))\n      :else (out-of-profile {:value v}))\n\n    ;; A byte string decodes to its bytes — major 2 carries no other\n    ;; meaning in this profile.  The tags guard rejects CborBigInt, which\n    ;; extends CborBytes but rides tags 2/3; that value has no producer\n    ;; here and is out of profile.\n    (dart/is? v cbor/CborBytes)\n    (if (no-tags? v)\n      (Uint8List.fromList (.-bytes v))\n      (out-of-profile {:value v}))\n\n    (dart/is? v cbor/CborList)\n    (cond\n      (no-tags? v) (mapv from-cbor v)\n      (only-tag? v 258) (into #{} (map from-cbor) v)\n      (only-tag? v 27) (from-named-frame (nth v 0) (nth v 1))\n      :else (out-of-profile {:value v}))\n\n    (dart/is? v cbor/CborMap)\n    (if (no-tags? v)\n      (into {}\n            (map (fn [entry] [(from-cbor (key entry)) (from-cbor (val entry))]))\n            v)\n      (out-of-profile {:value v}))\n\n    :else (out-of-profile {:value v})))\n\n\n(defn decode\n  \"Decode exactly one canonical CBOR item into the portable domain.\n\n   The trailing byte-compare is the duplicate-map-key guard: the package\n   collapses duplicate keys while materializing Dart Maps, and this is the\n   only point where the collapse is observable.\"\n  [bytes]\n  (let [tree (cbor/cborDecode bytes)\n        value (from-cbor tree)]\n    (when-not (bytes= bytes (encode value))\n      (out-of-profile {:reason :non-canonical-or-duplicate}))\n    value))\ndocs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:487:`dao.stream.transit-json` (text frames) and `dao.stream.cbor` (binary\ndocs/design/dao.jing.md:477:  digests) as a CBOR byte string on the `dao.stream.cbor` profile and as a\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md:186:| rows and vectors materialized in `dao.jing`; `:yin.code/hash` written | §2.1, §4.1, UCF §7.3.2 | D3 answered (individual rows); the intake-stream metadata issue is resolved by D7 (dao.stream.cbor) | U10 |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md:433:### D7 — metadata on the intake stream [Owner: additive dao.stream.cbor protocol, reject base64, 2026-09-18]\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md:435:The owner rejects wrapping CBOR in Base64 Transit. Instead, a new `dao.stream.cbor` wire protocol will be built additively alongside the existing `dao.stream.transit-json`. The REPL and intake streams can switch to this new binary WebSocket protocol to natively preserve metadata, without breaking existing Transit API clients. `dao.jing.cbor` can seamlessly run on top of whichever underlying stream protocol is active.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md:592:**U10a — Stream Codec Parameterization & dao.stream.cbor (D7).** Parameterize the single `dao.stream.ws` state machine with an explicit codec profile containing the subprotocol name, frame kind, value-domain predicate, encoder, and decoder. Preserve `dao.stream.transit-json` and its text-wire behavior unchanged. Upgrade the JVM, browser, Node, and Dart adapters to send and receive typed text/binary messages without content sniffing or NUL sentinels. Add deterministic dual-subprotocol negotiation: the attaching composition explicitly selects a profile; an endpoint may serve the same logical-stream identity concurrently through either profile; no silent downgrade is permitted. Preserve the existing envelopes and lifecycle.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md:597:**U10 — content in `dao.jing` (D3 answered: individual rows; D7 answered: additive dao.stream.cbor binary websockets).** Rows and\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md:720:| D7 intake stream metadata | U10 | done | **answered 2026-09-18**: Reject Base64 Transit wrap. Additively build `dao.stream.cbor` binary WebSocket protocol alongside Transit. |\ntest/dao/jing/stream_test.cljc:4:   string on `dao.stream.cbor`, as the named vector of octets on\ntest/dao/jing/stream_test.cljc:10:            [dao.stream.cbor :as cbor]\ntest/dao/jing/stream_test.cljc:43:            wrapped (jing-stream/wrap-bytes cbor/profile bs)]\ntest