 byte-level contract both implement is `dao.stream.cbor.boring`'s doc.\"\n./src/cljc/dao/stream/cbor.cljc:22:               :default [dao.stream.cbor.boring :as impl])))\n./src/cljc/dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc:1:(ns dao.stream.cbor.boring\n./src/cljc/dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc:27:        :default [[boring.core :as boring]])))\n./src/cljc/dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc:177:     (boring/encode (rewrite value) opts)))\n./src/cljc/dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc:205:     (let [items (boring/decode-seq bytes decode-opts)]\n./docs/orchestrator-log.md:4180:named frames; boring's native tag-39 arm rejected entirely — eliminates a\n./docs/orchestrator-log.md:4197:against primary sources (Clojars: boring 0.1.30 latest, 2026-09-06;\n./public/chp/blog/architecture.blog:705:           \"The simplification: If you use Datom.World, your Polylith structure becomes incredibly boring. \"\n./docs/design/dao.space.schema.md:74:neighboring interpreter point that changes exactly one thing — the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
