toms accrete. `dao.stream` is the vessels that carry them; `dao.space` is the metabolism of the leaves. The **system** is the **Metabolic Fibration**: streams lift raw bits into $d_5$, the heartwood holds them, and the leaves' chloroplasts (`dao.space.query`) project them into a living world of coexisting views.\ntest/dao/jing/dht_test.cljc:1:(ns dao.jing.dht-test\ntest/dao/jing/dht_test.cljc:2:  \"Contract tests for the dao.jing.dht content-store backend\ntest/dao/jing/dht_test.cljc:3:   (docs/design/dao.jing.md): strict content addressing, best-effort\ntest/dao/jing/dht_test.cljc:5:   full-mesh FakeNet grid of dao.jing.mem/create-content-mem locals.\ntest/dao/jing/dht_test.cljc:11:            [dao.jing :as jing]\ntest/dao/jing/dht_test.cljc:12:            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\ntest/dao/jing/dht_test.cljc:13:            [dao.jing.dht :as dht]\ntest/dao/jing/dht_test.cljc:14:            [dao.jing.dht.kad :as kad]\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:8:provenance-free; `dao.space.query/q` runs over the rows directly; all `yin.vm` evaluators are `dao.stream` observers that load rows to evaluate code; concurrently, a dedicated AST indexer observes the same stream and maintains the **row relation** of §6.1 (the `$ast` relation `q` runs over) from the rows it observes. `dao.jing` is the content store the rows already live in; it is not the indexer's output; code on a stream is rows end to end; `t` and `m` live in a ledger of\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:26:expansion event), [`dao.jing.md`](./dao.jing.md) (content addressing and\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:45:| **Content**    | `{:type :lambda :params [x]…}`,| The Map AST code itself, stored as  | the content        | `dao.jing`, under its    | immutable; no `t`, no `m`, no  |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:121:  else about the code; two ledgers that agree on `dao.jing` addresses\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:179:`(dao.jing/segment-key body)` (`src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:217-225`). The sto