ed with `dao.jing` functions exactly as a vector database.**\ndocs/design/dao.field.md:20:If you bundle the two together, you have durable storage (`dao.jing`), an ingestion path (`dao.stream`), and an index/query layer that performs similarity search (`dao.field`). To a consumer, it fulfills all the requirements and use cases of a vector database. The architectural distinction is composability: instead of a monolithic silo that only understands vectors, it is a vector database constructed dynamically over a universal tuple store—meaning those exact same vectors can simultaneously be queried as a discrete tuple space via `dao.space`.\ndocs/design/dao.field.md:29:materializations in `dao.jing`, and `dao.jing` privileges neither. Exact\ndocs/design/dao.field.md:50:- `docs/design/dao.jing.md` — the storage boundary both read: the content-addressed store of opaque bytes served as content, never as datoms\ndocs/design/dao.field.md:100:`dao.jing`. It is pure: pull the `d_k` tuples, build a proximity index, answer. It owns no\ndocs/design/dao.field.md:124:the metric one, because they read the same `dao.jing`.\ndocs/design/dao.field.md:145:`dao.space`: same `dao.jing`, a different space made from the same n-tuples.\ndocs/design/dao.field.md:150:storage and log traditions (Datomic, Plan 9) live in [`dao.jing`](dao.jing.md) and\ndocs/design/dao.field.md:158:reads the same `dao.jing` tuples as `d_k` coordinates and agents coordinate by the geometric proximity\ndocs/design/dao.stream.discovery.md:15:- `docs/design/dao.jing.md` — the content-addressed storage observer\ndocs/design/dao.stream.discovery.md:16:- `docs/design/dao.jing.dht.md` — Kademlia backend; sortition and Sybil open questions\ndocs/design/dao.stream.discovery.md:131:sortition/Sybil-resistance research program `dao.jing.dht.md` already flags. Most\ndocs/design/dao.stream.discovery.md:225:   mutable DaoJing state; see `dao.jing.dht.md`) — mechanism (1) *is* this\ndocs/design/dao.space.md:4:that emerges** when agen